          %h3#for_schemes For schemes
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ThomasonTrobaugh90"} Thomason-Trobaugh 90
          %h4#quillen_ktheory Quillen K-theory
          %p
            The Quillen K-theory of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is defined as the algebraic K-theory of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (using the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+Q-construction"} Quillen Q-construction
          %h4#thomasontrobaugh_ktheory Thomason-Trobaugh K-theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Perf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Perf(X)
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+complexes"} perfect complexes
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is defined via the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+S-construction"} Waldhausen S-construction
          %p
            It may also be defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} K-theory of a stable (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Perf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Perf(X)
            viewed as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
          %p
            Thomason-Trobaugh K-theory coincides with Quillen K-theory for schemes that admit an ample family of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
          %h3#for_smooth_manifolds For smooth manifolds
          %p
            Discussion of algebraic K-theory as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectrum"} smooth spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mi op
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Spectra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothMfd^{op} \longrightarrow Spectra
            via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto K(C^\infty(X))
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Voelkl 13
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Bunke14"} Bunke 14
          %p For more on this see at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory+of+smooth+manifolds"} algebraic K-theory of smooth manifolds
            %li
