          %h2#examples_2 Examples
          %h3#OnMonoidalStacks On monoidal stacks
          %p
            Algebraic K-theory is traditionally applied to single
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} functorial
            it may just as well be applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            with values in these.
          %p
            Notably, applied to the monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            (with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} K-theory of a monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+spectra"} sheaf of spectra
            which is a form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            spectrum. For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential%20cohomology%20diagram#DifferentialKTheory"} differential cohomology hexagon – Differential K-theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg+swindle"} Eilenberg swindle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+algebraic+K-theory"} equivariant algebraic K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+algebraic+K-theory"} iterated algebraic K-theory
          %p Types of categories for which a theory of algebraic K-theory exist include notably the notions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"}> Quillen exact category
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"}> abelian category
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"}> Waldhausen category
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"}> triangulated category
                \.
          %p Concrete examples of interest include for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the category of finitely generated
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+unital+algebra"} algebra
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaves
                over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noetherian+ring"} noetherian
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %li
              %p the category of locally free sheaves over a scheme,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gersten+resolution"} Gersten resolution
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Milnor's K2
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Milnor%27s+K2"} ?
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steinberg+group"}> Steinberg group
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+central+extension"} universal central extension
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  higher algebraic K-theory
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/higher+algebraic+K-theory"} ?
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"} Quillen exact category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+Q-construction"} Quillen's Q-construction
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+S-construction"} Waldhausen S-construction
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volodin+spaces"} Volodin spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+cyclic+homology"}> topological cyclic homology
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory+of+operator+algebras"} algebraic K-theory of operator algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulator"} Beilinson regulator
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+algebraic+K-theory"} differential algebraic K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-connective+algebraic+K-theory"} non-connective algebraic K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+algebraic+K-theory"} real algebraic K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+algebraic+K-theory"} bivariant algebraic K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-motive"} K-motive
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/red-shift+conjecture"} red-shift conjecture
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtrations+on+algebraic+K-theory"} filtrations on algebraic K-theory
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th geometric context
                  %th
                    universal additive
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+cohomology+theory"} bivariant
                    (preserves
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequences"} split exact sequences
                  %th
                    universal localizing
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+cohomology"} bivariant
